    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="0625" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4920: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harris</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">temporarily at Omsk</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-05T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Morris.</p>
                <p>Your July 24, 4 p.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d550-f1"/> Department believes it
                    would be a serious step, militating definitely against the purpose of the
                    Associated Governments to assist Russia in Siberia, were
                        Semenoff promoted to a full generalship. If you deem it
                    advisable you may say this emphatically both to Kolchak and to Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
